{% extends "layout/base.njk" %}

{% block content %}

<!-- Hero -->
<section class="dest-page-hero" id="top">

  <div class="dest-page-hero__img">
    <picture>
      <source srcset="/images/photos/dcl-fantasy-ship-hero.webp?v={{ site.assetVersion }}" type="image/webp">
      <img
        class="dest-page-hero__photo"
        src="/images/photos/dcl-fantasy-ship-hero.jpg?v={{ site.assetVersion }}"
        alt="Disney Fantasy cruise ship docked at a tropical port"
        width="2400"
        height="1350"
        fetchpriority="high"
      >
    </picture>
  </div>
  <div class="dest-page-hero__overlay"></div>

  <nav class="dest-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <div class="dest-breadcrumb__inner">
      <a href="/" class="dest-breadcrumb__link">Home</a>
      <span class="dest-breadcrumb__sep">&rsaquo;</span>
      <span class="dest-breadcrumb__current">Disney Cruise Line</span>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <div class="dest-page-hero__content">
    <p class="section-eyebrow">Disney Cruise Line</p>
    <h1 class="dest-page-hero__headline">
      Disney magic<br>
      on the <em>open ocean.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="dest-page-hero__sub">
      Smaller ships. Extraordinary service. Characters who learn your children's names. I've sailed Disney Cruise Line with my family — and I'll help you decide when DCL is the right fit (and when another line is actually better).
    </p>
    <a href="{{ site.links.consultation }}" class="btn btn--gold">
      Start Your Escape
    </a>
  </div>

</section>

<!-- Intro -->
<section class="dest-intro">
  <div class="dest-intro__inner">
    <p class="dest-intro__lead">
      Disney Cruise Line is what happens when Disney applies its obsession with storytelling and detail to a ship. The experience is intimate, family-first, and completely different from the big mainstream lines.
    </p>
    <p class="dest-intro__body">
      I've cruised Norwegian and Disney Cruise Line as well as Royal Caribbean. DCL costs more — and it's worth it for the right family. My job is to tell you honestly when Royal is the smarter choice for your trip, and when nothing else matches what DCL delivers.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Personal Story -->
<section class="dest-story" id="our-experience">
  <div class="dest-story__inner">

    <div class="dest-story__text">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">Our Experience</p>
      <h2 class="dest-story__headline">
        When Disney does<br>
        <em>everything.</em>
      </h2>
      <p class="dest-story__body">
        On Disney Fantasy, the crew learned our kids' names by day two. Character meets weren't a frantic park queue — they were real moments on the ship. Rotational dining, Castaway Cay, and the kids' clubs are designed so parents actually get adult time without guilt.
      </p>
      <p class="dest-story__body">
        The ships are smaller and more intimate than Royal Caribbean. The service is genuinely different. The entertainment, the character experiences, and the attention to family-specific detail put DCL in its own category — not a "Disney-themed" cruise, but a cruise built around how families actually travel.
      </p>
      <p class="dest-story__body">
        But when DCL is the right fit, there's nothing else like it. The kids talk about it for years. I'll help you match ship, itinerary, cabin category, and port timing — and pair a sailing with Walt Disney World when that combination makes sense.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="dest-story__photo">
      <picture>
        <source srcset="/images/photos/dcl-jasmine-meet-story.webp?v={{ site.assetVersion }}" type="image/webp">
        <img
          src="/images/photos/dcl-jasmine-meet-story.jpg?v={{ site.assetVersion }}"
          alt="Family character meet with Princess Jasmine in the Disney Fantasy atrium"
          loading="lazy"
          width="1600"
          height="1200"
        >
      </picture>
      <figcaption class="dest-story__caption">Disney Fantasy — character meet in the atrium</figcaption>
    </figure>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- Why DCL -->
<section class="dest-detail">
  <div class="dest-detail__inner">
    <p class="section-eyebrow">Why Disney Cruise Line</p>
    <h2 class="dest-detail__headline">
      What I help you <em>get right.</em>
    </h2>
    <div class="dest-detail__grid">
      <article class="dest-detail__item">
        <h3 class="dest-detail__title">Is DCL the right line?</h3>
        <p class="dest-detail__body">
          Age of kids, thrill level, budget, and whether you're combining with Disney World — I'll tell you straight when Royal or another line fits better, and when DCL is worth the premium.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="dest-detail__item">
        <h3 class="dest-detail__title">Ship &amp; itinerary</h3>
        <p class="dest-detail__body">
          Fantasy-class ships, shorter Bahamas sailings, longer Caribbean loops — length and ports change the rhythm of the whole trip. I'll match itinerary to how your family actually uses sea days and port days.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="dest-detail__item">
        <h3 class="dest-detail__title">Cabin &amp; concierge</h3>
        <p class="dest-detail__body">
          Inside, ocean view, verandah, or concierge — I'll explain when concierge truly pays off (milestone trips, multigen groups) and when a well-placed verandah is enough.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="dest-detail__item">
        <h3 class="dest-detail__title">World + cruise combos</h3>
        <p class="dest-detail__body">
          Port Canaveral makes a WDW + 3-night cruise one of the best family weeks in travel. I'll help you sequence parks, resort, and sailing so you're not exhausted by day three.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Insider Tips -->
<section class="dest-tips" id="tips">
  <div class="dest-tips__inner">

    <div class="dest-tips__header">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">What I've Learned</p>
      <h2 class="dest-tips__headline">
        Insider tips for<br>
        <em>first-time</em> DCL families.
      </h2>
      <p class="dest-tips__intro">
        Practical notes from our Disney Fantasy sailing — the kind of detail that doesn't show up in a brochure.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="dest-tips__grid">

      <article class="dest-tip">
        <span class="dest-tip__num">01</span>
        <h3 class="dest-tip__title">Port Canaveral Is the Easiest Start</h3>
        <p class="dest-tip__body">If you're driving from Florida or extending a Disney World stay, Port Canaveral is smooth, fast, and close to Orlando. Pair a 3-night cruise with a 4-night park stay and you have an unforgettable 7-day trip.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="dest-tip">
        <span class="dest-tip__num">02</span>
        <h3 class="dest-tip__title">Castaway Cay Is Its Own Experience</h3>
        <p class="dest-tip__body">Disney's private island has a family beach, an adults-only beach, and a dedicated teen section. The barbecue lunch is included. It's consistently the favorite day of the cruise for families — and it's only accessible on Disney sailings.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="dest-tip">
        <span class="dest-tip__num">03</span>
        <h3 class="dest-tip__title">Book Dining Rotations on Day One</h3>
        <p class="dest-tip__body">DCL's rotational dining — same group, different restaurant each night, your crew moves with you — is unique. Some restaurants are significantly better suited to different ages. I'll tell you which ones to prioritize for your family.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="dest-tip">
        <span class="dest-tip__num">04</span>
        <h3 class="dest-tip__title">Character Meets Are Less Chaotic Than the Parks</h3>
        <p class="dest-tip__body">On the ship, character availability is far more accessible than in any theme park. Your kids will have real moments with their favorite characters — not a frantic 90-minute queue. This alone is reason enough for some families to choose DCL.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="dest-tip">
        <span class="dest-tip__num">05</span>
        <h3 class="dest-tip__title">The Adult Areas Are Genuinely Adult</h3>
        <p class="dest-tip__body">DCL's kids' clubs are so good that kids actually want to go — which means you get real adult time. The adult-only pool, restaurant, and entertainment spaces are excellent. You can have a romantic evening while your kids have the time of their lives.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="dest-tip">
        <span class="dest-tip__num">06</span>
        <h3 class="dest-tip__title">Concierge Level: Worth It in Specific Scenarios</h3>
        <p class="dest-tip__body">Concierge provides dedicated service, priority boarding, and better room locations. I'll tell you honestly when it's worth the premium — milestone trips, multigenerational groups, or certain itineraries where access truly matters — and when it isn't.</p>
      </article>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Gallery -->
<section class="dest-gallery" id="gallery">
  <div class="dest-gallery__inner">

    <div class="dest-gallery__header">
      <h2 class="dest-gallery__headline">On board &amp; ashore</h2>
      <p class="dest-gallery__note">Family moments from our Disney Fantasy sailing</p>
    </div>

    <div class="dest-gallery__grid dest-gallery__grid--duo">
      <figure class="dest-gallery__item">
        <picture>
          <source srcset="/images/photos/dcl-frozen-meet-story.webp?v={{ site.assetVersion }}" type="image/webp">
          <img
            src="/images/photos/dcl-frozen-meet-story.jpg?v={{ site.assetVersion }}"
            alt="Character meet with Anna and Elsa on Disney Cruise Line"
            loading="lazy"
            width="1600"
            height="1200"
          >
        </picture>
      </figure>
      <figure class="dest-gallery__item dest-gallery__item--fit-contain">
        <picture>
          <source srcset="/images/photos/dcl-port-day-story.webp?v={{ site.assetVersion }}" type="image/webp">
          <img
            src="/images/photos/dcl-port-day-story.jpg?v={{ site.assetVersion }}"
            alt="Family at a tropical port with the Disney Fantasy in the background"
            loading="lazy"
            width="1600"
            height="1200"
          >
        </picture>
      </figure>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

{% include "partials/cta-strip.njk" %}

{% endblock %}